From 2935065b3f54f802fc20837b81ed7b7ed02b96ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:11:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(project_run): retire the session's previous server
 before EVERY launch

Red: a-server-that-outlives-its-round.test.ts
  "a retirement exists and runs before the launch" (launch index -1).
Culprits: aa64954a turned the launch into a managed child
(ExecutionGateway.startManaged) - pinned text only. 76f66a5d then added
a second launch, the dependency-free records bundle, ABOVE the single
retireRecordedServer call, so that path started a new preview beside the
session's live previous one and overwrote its record: an orphan no later
round can find - the exact failure this guard was written for.

Decision: P for the spelling (aa64954a), R for the new launch path
(76f66a5d). The one retirement call now sits right after stopServer and
after the adoption return, before every launch (records bundle, managed
launch, verified-bundle fallback). Preflight failures between the two
positions now also retire the recorded server, matching what stopServer
already did there for in-memory servers.

Guards: the static order is asserted against all three launches, and two
behavioural tests run the real tool on real processes: a live previous
preview recorded in joeProjects, then project_run on (a) a dependency-free
records bundle and (b) a managed `node server.js` project.

Evidence before the fix (unchanged production code):
  x a retirement exists... "launch": "startStaticBuildPreview(dependencyFreeBundle, port)",
    - "retiredFirst": true, + "retiredFirst": false
  x a dependency-free records bundle does not start beside the previous preview
    Expected value: "retired previous server pid=19996 port=1"
    Received array: ["project_run: ignored stale or unowned live record (http://127.0.0.1:1/)",
    "project_run: serving dependency-free records bundle (.../next-app/dist)",
    "The dependency-free local records app is live - preview: http://127.0.0.1:32887/"]
  v ...and neither does a managed server (770 ms)
After: 8/8 in the file; project-run.test.ts and
a-preview-that-outlives-every-round.test.ts green; tsc --noEmit exit 0.
Line endings preserved (numstat == --ignore-cr-at-eol numstat).

